  "text": "Stanly County Board of Elections\ntop of page\nHOME\nABOUT US\nMEET THE BOARD\nOFFICE STAFF\nWHAT WE DO\n2026 MEETING SCHEDULE\nREGISTER\nVOTING\nEARLY VOTING\nBY MAIL\nMILITARY/OVERSEAS\nELECTION DAY\nINFORMATION\nCAMPAIGNING & SIGN REGULATIONS\nPARTY CONTACTS\nINFO FOR CANDIDATES\nELECTED OFFICIALS\nMAPS\nSTATS & HISTORY\nREQUEST PUBLIC INFORMATION\nGET INVOLVED\nELECTION DAY\nSTUDENT ASSISTANTS\nEARLY VOTING\nMAT\nMore\nUse tab to navigate through the menu items.\nLog In\nRegister to Vote\nPolling Place Search\nVoter ID Information\nMy Representatives\nCampaign Finance Reports\nNovember 3, 2026 General Election Important Dates\nRequested Absentee By-Mail Ballots Being Mailed Begins:\nSeptember 4, 2026\n*Registration Deadline\n(to vote on by mail or on Election Day):\nOctober 9, 2026\nEarly Voting Begins:\nOctober 15, 2026\nDeadline to Request Absentee By-Mail Ballot:\nOctober 20, 2026\nSick & Disabled Ballot Requests Begin:\nOctober 21, 2026\nEarly Voting Ends:\nOctober 31, 2026\nDeadline to Request a Voter Photo ID:\nOctober 31, 2026\nSick & Disabled Ballot Request Deadline:\nNovember 2, 2026\nElection Day:\nNovember 3, 2026\nDeadline for Absentee By-Mail Ballots to be Received by Board of Elections Office:\nNovember 3, 2026\nDeadline to Receive UOCAVA Ballots:\nNovember 12, 2026\nElection Results Made Official (Canvass):\nNovember 13, 2026\n\u200b\n\u200b\n\u200b\nGeneral Election Voter Guide\n*Voters that miss the October 9th registration deadline, may register and vote during the early voting period, but must provide additional ID documents. See\nSame Day Registration Information\nto learn more.\nSample Ballot Information\nA voter's address will determine which contests appear on the ballot they receive. To view your sample ballot, use the 'View My Sample Ballot' button below and search your voter record. Select your name and scroll down to the sample ballot section of your profile.\nView My Sample Ballot\nPer NCGS 147-54.10 the Secretary of State is required to release a summary explanation of Constitutional Amendment questions that will appear on the ballot. The summaries prepared by the Legislative Services Officer can be viewed using the 'View Summary Explanation of 2026 Constitutional Amendments' button below.\nView Summary of 2026 Constitutional Amendments\nThe online\nJudicial Voter Guide: 2026 General Election\nis now available\non the State Board of Elections\u2019 website.\nThe digital guide contains information about this year\u2019s candidates for North Carolina\u2019s appellate courts \u2013 the North Carolina Supreme Court and North Carolina Court of Appeals.\nEarly Voting Information\nLocations\nStanly County Commons\nDSS Auditorium\n1000 N. 1st Street, Albemarle, NC 28001\nLocust Town Center\nJoel Huneycutt Community Rm.\n186 Ray Kennedy Drive, Locust, NC 28097\nDates & Times\nOctober 15th - October 31st\nOpen Weekdays: 8:00 a.m. - 7:30 p.m.\nSaturday, October 31st: 8:00 a.m. - 3:00 p.m.\nEarly Voting Turnout Statistics\n*Statistics are posted daily after the early voting sites close and reconciliation is complete.\nGeneral Election Public Notices\nNotice of Early Voting Buffer Zones\nNotice of Election Day Buffer Zones\nUOCAVA Election Notice\nNotice of Election\nAbsentee Meeting Schedule\nAbsentee Count Resolution\nNC Registration Repair Project\nThe Registration Repair Project is an effort by the State Board of Elections to collect identification numbers from registered voters who do not have an N.C. driver\u2019s license/DMV ID number or social security number in the state\u2019s voter registration database. These numbers are used to verify that registrants are who they claim to be. Voters who do not have this information in their record may need to cast a provisional ballot and provide this information the next time they vote.\n\u200b\n\u200b\nThe voters who have not provided the required information have been notified by mail of the missing information.\nSearch Registration Repair Voters\nTo avoid any potential problems at the polls and to ensure all votes are counted, the State Board strongly encourages voters who receive letters to provide their identification numbers in one of the three ways:\nOnline\nIn-Person\nBy Mail\nFor more details on the Registration Repair project, the NC State Board of Elections has created a dedicated webpage with the most current information. Visit\nhttps://www.ncsbe.gov/registrationrepair\nSubscribe\nGet exclusive updates, election related reminders, and issues of our newsletter sent straight to your inbox.\nEmail\n*\nJoin Our Mailing List\nBoard Meetings\nMeeting Schedule\nView the agendas, review previous meeting minutes, or listen live to the board meetings using the Zoom link provided in the Board Meeting Schedule.\nElection Day and Early Voting Officials Needed!\nOfficials will check-in voters, issue ballots, and ensure the conduct at each voting site is fair, impartial, and in accordance with current election laws.\nVisit the\nGet Involved page\nfor more information.\nApply Now\nFirst name\n*\nLast name\n*\nEmail\n*\nPhone\nLong answer\n*\nSubmit\nContact Us\nMAIL:\nEMAIL:\nPHONE:\nPO Box 1309, Albemarle, NC 28002\n[email protected]\n704-986-3647\nIN PERSON:\n1000 N. 1st Street, Albemarle, NC 28001\nCopyright \u00a9 2017 Official Website of the Stanly County Board of Elections.\nTerms of Service\n-\nPrivacy Statement\nInformation Disclaimer\nEndorsement Disclaimer: Pop-Ups\nEndorsement Disclaimer: Links\nbottom of page",
